    "updated_at": "2023-05-08T05:29:16Z",
    "body": "Thanks for opening,\r\n\r\nUsing `AbortSignal.any([signal])` just to use the fact it exposes an underlying different mechanism in the DOM seems like not a great design. It's similar to making a dummy hanging `fetch` request and `.catch`ing it to know cancellation happened.\r\n\r\nI'm trying to get around having _another way_ to dispatch things, @smaug---- can you elaborate what specifically about not being able to prevent other listeners from running bothers you?",
